If you ntpdate at startup, your system clock will be set to the date you get 
via ntp regardless of skew.  Put the following in /etc/rc.conf:

ntp_enable="YES"
ntp_flags="-b ntp.server.here"
ntpd_enable="YES"

That should get you set up :>

Dave

